{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Rain</b> — Now the sense of \"Elohim, when You went out before Your people\" is to recount the beginning of Israel's triumph." "<b>And the word תניף</b> — [means] You watered it, as in: \"My bed was moist [נפתי משכבי].\"" "<b>Your heritage</b> — It is the land of Israel, and the sense is that HaShem waters it forever, in the manner of: \"The eyes of YHWH your Elohim are always upon it.\"" "<b>And the sense of ונלאה</b> — As though it were exhausted [נלאה], You established it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:04.776886069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}